<Layout title="Drylining Dunfermline | Partition Walls &amp; Ceilings Contractors" description="Professional drylining contractors in Dunfermline. Expert partition walls, suspended ceilings, and plasterboard installation for Dunfermline, Fife, and the wider KY1–KY18 postcode region. Free quotes." canonical="/areas/dunfermline/" schema={schema}>
  <section style="position:relative;min-height:400px;display:flex;align-items:center;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#1a1a2e 0%,#16213e 100%);overflow:hidden;"> <img src="/images/hero-main.jpg" alt="Drylining services in Dunfermline and Fife" style="position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;opacity:0.25;"> <div class="container" style="position:relative;z-index:1;text-align:center;padding:60px 20px;"> <nav style="font-size:13px;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.70);margin-bottom:12px;"> <a href="/" style="text-decoration:none;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.70);">Home</a> / <a href="/areas/" style="text-decoration:none;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.70);">Areas</a> / <span style="color:#ffffff;">Drylining in Dunfermline</span> </nav> <h1 style="font-size:clamp(28px,4vw,44px);font-weight:800;color:#ffffff;margin-bottom:14px;line-height:1.15;">Drylining in Dunfermline</h1> <p style="font-size:17px;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.85);max-width:700px;margin:0 auto;line-height:1.6;">CSCS-accredited drylining contractors delivering partition walls, suspended ceilings, and plasterboard across Dunfermline, Fife, and the wider KY1–KY18 postcode region.</p> </div> </section> <section class="section"><div class="container" style="max-width:900px;"> <div style="padding:24px;margin-bottom:24px;border-left:4px solid var(--primary);background:var(--white);border-radius:var(--radius);border:1px solid var(--border);"> <p style="margin:0;font-size:15px;color:var(--text);"><strong>TL;DR:</strong> Drylining Dunfermline provides drylining, partition walls, and suspended ceilings across Dunfermline (KY1–KY12), Fife, and the wider area. Experienced with Abbey town properties, new residential developments, and commercial refurbishments in Fife's historic capital.</p> </div> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Drylining Services in Dunfermline</h2> <p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Dunfermline is Fife's historic capital, situated approximately 15 miles west of Edinburgh city centre. The KY1–KY12 postcode areas cover the town centre dominated by Dunfermline Abbey and Queen Anne's Palace, surrounding residential areas, and the wider Fife region. Dunfermline has a population of around 53,000 and serves as the commercial and cultural heart of West Fife. As Fife's largest town, it has experienced significant development including the Northshire development, retail expansions, and ongoing regeneration of the town centre. The city's strong links to Edinburgh via the M90 motorway and rail connections create consistent demand for quality drylining services across the Fife region, serving everything from the historic Abbey area to new build estates across the wider KY postcodes.</p> <p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">The area offers a distinctive mix of projects for our drylining team — from the careful internal refurbishment of listed properties near Dunfermline Abbey to large-scale new build residential and commercial developments. We cover the entire KY postcode region, serving everything from single-room domestic projects in period properties to larger commercial fit-outs along the town centre and business parks. All work is carried out to Scottish Building Standards compliant with all relevant sections.</p> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">What We Do in Dunfermline</h2> <p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Our Dunfermline crew handles everything from historic Abbey area property conversions to large-scale new build drylining — covering partition walls, suspended ceilings, and fire-rated wall systems across the KY postcode region.</p> <ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;font-size:1.0625rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;"> <li><strong>Historic property drylining</strong> — Internal wall insulation, room conversions, and partition walls in Dunfermline's listed properties near the Abbey, Queen Anne's Palace, and the Old Town area</li> <li><strong>New build drylining</strong> — Pre-completion drylining for large-scale residential developments across the Northshire, City Centre, and wider Fife areas</li> <li><strong>Commercial fit-outs</strong> — Office refurbs, retail units, and hospitality venues along Dunfermline town centre, King Street, and commercial parks</li> <li><strong>Fire-rated walls</strong> — Multi-storey residential and commercial buildings requiring Scottish Building Standards Section 2 (Fire) compliance with full documentation</li> <li><strong>Suspended ceilings</strong> — Commercial premises, offices, education facilities, and new build apartments across Fife</li> <li><strong>Acoustic partitions</strong> — Residential properties, student accommodation, and mixed-use developments in Dunfermline and surrounding Fife areas</li> </ul> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Areas of Dunfermline We Cover</h2> <ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;font-size:1.0625rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;"> <li>Dunfermline town centre (KY1) — King Street, South Street, Market Street</li> <li>Abbey area and Old Town (KY1)</li> <li>Culross Street and Park Place (KY1)</li> <li>Northshire development and King's Cross (KY11)</li> <li>Willowbrae and Lochgelly Road (KY12)</li> <li>Charlestown and Lochgelly (KY11/KY5)</li> <li>Alva and Lochgell (KY11)</li> <li>Kirkcaldy (KY1/KY2) — 15 minutes via A92</li> <li>Glenrothes (KY6/KY7) — 20 minutes via M90</li> <li>Fife area generally</li> </ul> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Dunfermline Building Regulations &amp; Planning</h2> <p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Dunfermline falls under <strong>Fife Council</strong> for building standards and planning. The town centre contains numerous Category A and B listed buildings, particularly those around Dunfermline Abbey and the Old Town that are within conservation areas. Internal structural alterations in listed buildings require listed building consent from the council. We work closely with clients, architects, and the council's building standards department to ensure every project — from a simple room partition in a historic property near the Abbey to a large-scale commercial fit-out at Northshire — is fully compliant with Scottish Building Standards and any additional conservation requirements.</p> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Why Choose Us for Dunfermline Projects</h2> <p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">As an Edinburgh-based drylining team, we have extensive experience working across Fife, including Dunfermline, Kirkcaldy, and Glenrothes. We understand the unique character of Dunfermline — from its historic Abbey and Old Town to the modern Northshire development and surrounding residential areas. Our crew is familiar with Scottish Building Standards and the particular requirements of working in Fife's historic capital. Whether you need drylining for a listed property near Dunfermline Abbey, a new build project, or a commercial refurbishment, our team delivers quality work on time and within budget.</p> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Related Services</h2> <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(180px,1fr));gap:10px;margin-bottom:1.5rem;"> <a href="/services/partition-walls/" style="text-decoration:none;padding:10px 14px;background:var(--white);border-radius:6px;font-size:14px;font-weight:600;border:1px solid var(--border);color:var(--text);">Partition Walls</a> <a href="/services/fire-rated-drylining/" style=